  "description": "Quartz.NET 4.x scheduling for AutoRegisterDependency, targeting net10.0 — the only framework Quartz 4.6 ships. Mark a component with [Component] and [Job(Cron = \"...\")]; a single RegisterQuartz4Async() call reads every job definition and builds the JobDetail and Trigger for each, and jobs are created through Quartz's Microsoft DI integration so [Autowired] / [Value] work as usual. Multiple cron expressions (separated by ';') produce one trigger per expression; missing or invalid cron skips only that job with a typed error. The scheduler is stopped and shut down with the host. Register the scheduler with Quartz's own builder.AddQuartz() / services.AddQuartz() — the former AddAutoRegisterQuartz4() helper no longer exists. Reference either this package or AutoRegisterDependency.Extension.Quartz3, never both.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
